        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="JMeg28QFHQqCXGKKknAn-140" parent="JMeg28QFHQqCXGKKknAn-138" style="swimlane;fontStyle=0;childLayout=stackLayout;horizontal=1;startSize=50;fillColor=none;horizontalStack=0;resizeParent=1;resizeParentMax=0;resizeLast=0;collapsible=0;marginBottom=0;html=1;foldingIconSize=20;strokeColor=default;swimlaneBody=1;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=14;fontColor=light-dark(#000000,#FFFFFF);" value="SUMMARY AND DEFINITION" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="1100" width="520" y="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="JMeg28QFHQqCXGKKknAn-141" parent="JMeg28QFHQqCXGKKknAn-140" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;Game Engines Manager&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Own multiple engines providing functionality who allow the simulation of a physical space.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Own a box2d world Object who hold a physic simulation space.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="170" width="520" y="50" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="JMeg28QFHQqCXGKKknAn-142" parent="JMeg28QFHQqCXGKKknAn-140" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Standardized Instance object :&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;Instance are pooled and indexed objects dynamically structured by a Set of Standard objects.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Instances can be synchonized with clone of themselves owned by another Thread.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Instance manager can save a group of Instance states and relation to a file. And can load later the same properties and relationship stucture&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;in another group of instances.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Runnables and Providers hold a single metodes and some tools to have many entities share them.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Standard are contructed by providing Runnables and Providers objects and by storing them in EventStacks for each Event if the lifecycle of an Instance (create, load, save, delete), or by mapping them to a key. Standards can be build recursivelly by copying or appendding other Standards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="370" width="520" y="220" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="JMeg28QFHQqCXGKKknAn-143" parent="JMeg28QFHQqCXGKKknAn-140" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;overflow=hidden;fontSize=10;horizontal=1;labelPosition=center;verticalLabelPosition=middle;align=left;strokeColor=none;spacingLeft=-25;spacingTop=-15;movable=1;resizable=1;rotatable=1;deletable=1;editable=1;locked=0;connectable=1;fontColor=light-dark(#000000,#CCCCCC);" value="&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Instance can store primitive values and arrays.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The stored object are accessed throug a Key.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Instances and Standards can be used for many different things while using objects of the same two class.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Standard define a specific set of Runnable and Provider (Run / Get / Got) and a Map to access them.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Standard define the creation and destruction process of Instances&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="130" width="520" y="590" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="JMeg28QFHQqCXGKKknAn-144" parent="JMeg28QFHQqCXGKKknAn-140" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;overflow=hidden;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h1 style=&quot;margin-top: 0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Engines Functionality :&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;The engines define a set of entity type. New entities are obtained from a common Pool. To create new entity Model Instance are used to provide the new object initial property. Models can be created, destroyed and modified in an asynchronous way.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;The collection of currently alive entities compose a game engine space. Filtered spacial query can be performed on the entities in a space. (Raycast)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Instance object provide ways to control the creation, destruction and activity of entity. They can also contain information about the current state of an entity specific property, or about a specific group of entity.&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(rgb(0, 0, 0), rgb(255, 255, 255));&quot;&gt;Executing a step is the simulation of the progression of the space entities property after a small constant duration. Entity relationship will also change to represent physical interaction. The beginning or end of an interactions between entity or the change of a value past a threshold can trigger the signalment of the event or the execution of a custom process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="380" width="520" y="720" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="JMeg28QFHQqCXGKKknAn-145" connectable="0" parent="JMeg28QFHQqCXGKKknAn-136" style="group;movable=0;resizable=0;rotatable=0;deletable=0;editable=0;locked=1;connectable=0;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="499.99923076923073" width="580" x="752" y="513" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
